  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reproductive Health Network Kenya (RHNK) is a network of over 500 trained health care providers across Kenya who are committed to the provision of comprehensive sexual and reproductive health and rights to all. The providers &#x2014; who include doctors, nurses, and midwives working in the private sector &#x2014; work together through this network to collaborate, build capacity, and advocate together for reproductive rights. RHNK has received support from Hewlett as a subgrantee under the Center for Reproductive Rights and also as the Self-Care Trailblazer Group led by Population Services International. This will be the first direct grant to RHNK and is aligned with the Global Reproductive Equity strategy. (Strategy: Global Reproductive Equity)</narrative>
  </description>
